## Key Analytical Notes

<div style="border-left:4px solid #EF4444;background:#FEF2F2;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#FEF2F2;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong>Loss-making 9M — margin deterioration</strong></span><br>
9MFY26 PAT swung to a <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">loss of ₹(66.61) crore</span>, versus a <span style="color:#22C55E;font-weight:600">profit of ₹10.83 crore</span> in the comparable 9MFY25 period per the same filing. This was driven by the <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">claims ratio rising from 67% to 74%</span> YoY, alongside a ₹2.01 crore one-off IRDAI penalty and a higher deferred-tax charge booked in Q3. The resulting <span style="color:#EF4444;font-weight:600">combined ratio of 110%</span> confirms underwriting losses are not being offset by investment income.
</div>

<div style="border-left:4px solid #F59E0B;background:#FFFBEB;padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<span style="background:#FFFBEB;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;"><strong>Solvency comfortable but thinning</strong></span><br>
Solvency ratio stands at <span style="color:#F59E0B;font-weight:600">1.70x</span> — above the regulatory minimum of 1.50x, but the buffer is narrower than typical for a well-capitalized health insurer, consistent with the capital drag from the 9M net loss.
</div>

### Data-Integrity Flags

- **GWP basis:** The Gross Direct Premium of <span style="color:#1E3A8A;font-weight:600">₹6,878.94 cr</span> reported in Form NL-4 reflects the statutory 1/n premium-recognition framework applicable from FY25-26 — the preferred basis per methodology; no conflicting ex-1/n figure appeared in this filing.
- **Retail health GWP / market share:** Not disclosed in statutory NL forms. The Health segment premium (₹6,609.78 cr) is a blended Retail+Group figure and was **not** used as a Retail-only proxy — left blank rather than estimated.
- **IFRS-basis PAT & Claims ratio:** IRDAI disclosures are prepared strictly under IGAAP; no IFRS figures are published in these statutory filings.
- **Expense ratio vs. EoM ratio:** NL-20 only publishes Expense-of-Management ratios (to Gross Direct Premium = 35%; to NWP = 36%); no separately labeled "Expense ratio" exists, so that row is intentionally blank to avoid conflating bases. Internal arithmetic checks out: Claims (74%) + Commission (18%) + implied expense component (~18%) ≈ Combined Ratio (110%).
- **Net worth reconciliation:** Two internally consistent measures exist in the filing — <span style="color:#1E3A8A;font-weight:600">₹2,622.4 cr</span> (excl. policyholders' fair-value change account) vs. ₹2,635.63 cr (incl. policyholders' FVC per Balance Sheet Total). The shareholders'-only figure (₹2,622.4 cr) is reported as the conventional "shareholders' equity" measure; a minor rounding gap versus the BVPS-derived cross-check (₹2,587.17 cr) likely stems from EPS/BVPS being rounded to 2 decimals in the ratios schedule.</ans>
